1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,650
Deep in pitch black space floats a giant planet without a sun.

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:08,280
Yet its sky burns with light ten thousand times stronger than Earth's.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:13,130
Meet SIMP J0136, a rogue world twelve times heavier than Jupiter.

4
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:17,220
It drifts twenty light-years away, completely untethered from any solar system.

5
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:21,300
Pause. Without a sun's solar wind, what powers these terrifying lights?

6
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:25,740
It generates its own magnetic field four million times stronger than Earth's.

7
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:29,830
This massive magnetosphere rips particles right out of empty interstellar space.

8
00:00:29,870 --> 00:00:34,250
Scientists suspect a hidden, volcanically active moon might be driving the charge.

9
00:00:34,290 --> 00:00:38,670
Just like Io feeds Jupiter, this unseen world creates a cosmic super-generator.

10
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:39,940
Proving that somewhere...
